- op: discuss  # 9f99
  at: '2026-10-25T20:08:23Z'  # 9f99
  by: agent  # 9f99
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9f99
  clock: 2  # 9f99
  nonce: 9f99  # 9f99
  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). CURRENT, WRONG VERDICT SHOWN. Shipped claim untrusted-input-no-database on Go: typed DB calls are withheld by the unclassified-call gate (net/http handler -> db.Exec, a typed *sql.DB parameter, gorm: all inconclusive); but fmt.Scanln -> package-global `var db *sql.DB; db.Exec(v)` reads confirmed_with_caveats (rc 3) whose only caveat is untyped_receiver -- implying typing would help, though go has no database sinks at all; a DB-free repo reads confirmed; on the same repos a code_execution claim reads inconclusive ('go has no sink in the code_execution zone'). Refs: _sink_zone_gaps cli.py:6796 (docstring premise :6804-6808, zone filter :6821-6825, per-language emptiness :6836); per-language sink count :7516-7519; shipped_non_boundary_sink_zones taint.py:2286; claim file lines unchanged. Zone list wider than filed: database also empty for javascript, typescript, bash; host_env and ipc also for groovy, bash; logging, network, subprocess for bash; network for haskell with --no-default-overlays. browser_storage is empty for every non-JS language by nature: the fix must rule whether a zone a language can never have withholds (the code_execution precedent says it does). P3 kept."  # 9f99
